and Embla...Scandinavia is rather untapped in Promethean...sounds promising.<br /> <br /> As for the dying-reborn gods, are there any with direct connections to plants? Or, really, any myths featuring human(oid)s and trees? I'm aiming for a Wasteland effect focusing heavily on plant life, either withering it or promoting rampant, out-of-control growth. Agriculture rebelling against mankind, and so on.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-26T16:46:25-07:00","id":149806,"title":"","content":"What about something like the <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nariphon\" target=\"_blank\">Nariphon</a>? A wasteland effect with the growth taking on humanoid appearance that plays on people's vices?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">A monster by any other name...</span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1204-bridgewarden","name":"BridgeWarden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1204_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-26T17:38:56-07:00","id":149865,"title":"","content":"Hmmm...give the story of Vessantara's wife and the Yogis a sufficiently WoD-ish twist, and I think we've got something. Add the attractive elements of the Galateids' sanguine nature with a more primal bent, include some variant origins with Ask and Embla, and the Mayan Wooden People...for a Pandoran, perhaps one of those man-eating plants that crop up in stories, or the traditional Mandrake...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}